  "necessity_paragraph": "The patient presents with recurrent episodes of palpitations and lightheadedness consistent with supraventricular tachycardia, accompanied by a recent history of transient cerebral ischemic attacks (I47.1, G45.9). Mobile cardiac telemetry (CPT 93229) is ordered to correlate these symptomatic events with underlying arrhythmias and to assess the efficacy of current rate-control therapy, which is medically necessary given the recurrent symptomatic presentation and the need to evaluate the arrhythmia responsible for the transient cerebral ischemic attacks."
